        "original_id": "20ad9018-2189-5d15-a0c0-f4f512d8da66",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Strongest Man in the World, Roving Mars, Now You See Him, Now You Don't, The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes\n- People: Kurt Russell, Winifred Deforest Coffin\n- Organizations: Disney\n- Places: Medfield College\n- Systems: Mars Exploration Rovers, Spirit, Opportunity\n- Topics: film sequels, documentary films, television appearances\n\nFacts:\n- The Computer Wore Tennis Shoes is a 1969 film that was later followed by the sequel Now You See Him, Now You Don't.\n- Now You See Him, Now You Don't was followed by the 1975 film The Strongest Man in the World.\n- The Strongest Man in the World is a 1975 Disney film starring Kurt Russell as still a student in the fictional Medfield College.\n- Winifred Deforest Coffin was an actress who appeared in the Hollywood film Now You See Him, Now You Don't.\n- Winifred Deforest Coffin also appeared in the television shows Adam-12, The Doris Day Show, The Debbie Reynolds Show, Lancer, The Beverly Hillbillies, High Chaparral, Death Valley Days, Petticoat Junction, Perry Mason, Bonanza, Bewitched, Honey West, and The Ann Sothern Show.\n- Roving Mars is an IMAX documentary film about the development, launch, and operation of the Mars Exploration Rovers Spirit and Opportunity.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
